Preprocessing source files (conditional compilation).
====================================================

Some Fortran source files in tfem have the extention .F90 instead of .f90.
These files are first scanned by the Fortran preprocessor (fpp) before being
compiled. Instructions in the .F90 file like,

#if MACRO
    statements1
#else
    statements2
#endif

will generate a different source depending on whether MACRO has been set
by the compiler option -DMACRO (statements1) or not (statements2). The compiler
options for the preprocessor need to be added to FPPFLAGS in the Mdefs.mk file.


The following macros can be set with the meaning in the second column:

Compile tfem:
------------

 NO_LIBHSL  Do not have a compiled HSL library with MA57, MA41 and EA23.
            Currently, this only affects how eigenvalues/vectors of
            3x3 matrices are computed.

 I8         TFEM is compiled with default integer being int64.
            Currently, this only affects UMFPACK.

Compile and run examples:
------------------------

 SKIT2      Sparskit2 is available and add-on sk_solve has been compiled.
            This only affects examples using sparskit.

 METIS5     Add-on metis5 has been compiled and the metis5 library has been
            added for linking. This only affects examples using metis5.

 PARDISO    Add-on pardiso has been compiled and the mkl library has been
            added for linking. This only affects examples using pardiso.

 MKL_GMRES  Add-on mkl_gmres has been compiled and the mkl library has been
            added for linking. This only affects examples using mkl_gmres.

 HSL_EXTRA  Add-on hsl_extra has been compiled and the libhsl3 library has been
            added for linking. This only affects examples using hsl_extra.

 PARTRACK   Add-on particle_tracking has been compiled and the nr library
            has been added for linking. This only affects examples using
            particle_tracking.

 UMFPACK    Add-on umfpack has been compiled and the umfpack library has been
            added for linking. This only affects examples using umfpack.

 FEAST      Add-on feast has been compiled and the feast library has been
            added for linking. This only affects examples using feast.


IMPORTANT notes:

- Nagfor requires the -fpp option to invoke the preprocessor for .F90 files.
  If you create an Mdefs.mk file from a recent Mdefs_distr.mk file, this is
  already set. Gfortran and Intel Fortran are triggered by the .F90 extension
  and no additional option is required to invoke the preprocessor.

- In macOS file names are case insensitive by default. Although name.f90 and
  name.F90 refer to the same file, compilers do pick up the different
  extension. Also "git mv name.f90 name.F90" works as expected. So, most things
  on application level work, but be careful:

     macbook:~ cp name.f90 name.F90
     cp: name.F90 and name.f90 are identical (not copied).
     macbook:~ ls name.*
     name.f90
     macbook:~ mv name.f90 name.F90
     macbook:~ ls name.*
     name.F90
     macbook:~ rm -i name.F90
     remove name.F90? n
     macbook:~ rm -i name.f90
     remove name.f90? y
     macbook:~ ls name.*
     ls: name.*: No such file or directory

  So a folder cannot contain two files name.f90 and name.F90 at the same time,
  since they refer to the same file.
